DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppaammaaddddnnooiissee  adds  the  specified  noise  type  to a Netpbm image.  ppaa‐‐
       mmaaddddnnooiissee treats a PPM image as 3 independent planes, not as a plane of
       colors in a color space.


OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In  addition  to  the options common to all programs based on libnetpbm
       (most notably --qquuiieett, see
        Common Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩  ),  ppaammaaddddnnooiissee  recognizes
       the following command line options:



       --llaammbbddaa _v_a_l_u_e
              This  is  the  expected  value of the Poisson distribution for a
              sample value
                of mximum intensity.  The expected value for other intensities
              is
                proportional; e.g. for half intensity, it is half this value.

              This is meaningful only with --ttyyppee==ppooiissssoonn.

              The default value is 12.


       --llssiiggmmaa _v_a_l_u_e
              Used for laplacian noise only.  The default value is 10.0.


       --mmggssiiggmmaa _v_a_l_u_e
              Used  for multiplicative gaussian noise only.  The default value
              is 0.5.


       --sseeeedd _i_n_t
              Used for all noise types.  Set the initial random number genera‐
              tor seed value.


       --ssiiggmmaa11 _v_a_l_u_e
              Used for gaussian noise only.  The default value is 4.0.


       --ssiiggmmaa22 _v_a_l_u_e
              Used for gaussian noise only.  The default value is 20.0.


       --ttoolleerraannccee _r_a_t_i_o
              Used  for  impulse noise only.  The default value is 0.10.  This
              means that 5% of all pixel values will be set to 0 and  5%  will
              be set to the maxval


       --ttyyppee _n_o_i_s_e___t_y_p_e
              Select  type  of  noise  by name.  The following noise types are
              available: gaussian,  multiplicative_gaussian,  impulse,  lapla‐
              cian,  poisson.   Only  enough letters to be unique are required
              for the noise type option.  The default noise type is ggaauussssiiaann.



